The work is actually a side issue, though at this point it's far from
insignificant.  The actual reason is that many of the changes are
themselves dependent on other changes to be properly balanced and/or
appreciated; for example, my incremental resistance model is extremely 
harsh if deadly poison is still an instakill.  Likewise, my upgrades 
to monster AC are nearly meaningless if players can still get +13 to hit
on a d20 simply by carrying a blessed luckstone.

What it comes down to is: I didn't design my changes to be individually 
applicable in piecemeal form, I designed them all as part of a greater 
whole, a single "vision" if you will.  Using only parts of that whole
will give an inaccurate perspective of the changes (see above); so, I
choose to only distribute it as "all or nothing".

